22ji|n|An American plant (Nicotiana Tabacum) of the Nightshade family, much used for smoking and chewing, and as snuff. As a medicine, it is narcotic, emetic, and cathartic. Tobacco has a strong, peculiar smell, and an acrid taste. ; The leaves of the plant prepared for smoking, chewing, etc., by being dried, cured, and manufactured in various ways.	v:1vkz,100,3;52y,52,3~52y,52,3;1vkz,100,3	V:1b06,111,3;26eh,10,4~26eh,10,4;1b06,111,3	n:1vkz,84,1;1xr,80,4;165r,12,5~165r,12,5;1xr,80,4;1vkz,84,1	N:1b06,115,4;1vkz,104,4;1vkq,91,4;20ya,86,4;15j4,86,3;1181,83,11;e5x,83,11;1jbw,74,4;15le,68,3;e62,50,2~e5x,83,11;1181,83,11;20ya,86,4;1vkq,91,4;1b06,115,4;1vkz,104,4;1jbw,74,4;15j4,86,3;15le,68,3;e62,50,2
