22q7|n|A mineral occurring in rhombic prisms, generally yellowish and pellucid, also colorless, and of greenesh, bluish, or brownish shades. It sometimes occurs massive and opaque. It is a fluosilicate of alumina, and is used as a gem. ; Either one of two species of large, brilliantly colored humming birds of the Topaza, of South America and the West Indies.	N:1sg,88,3~1sg,88,3
22qa|n|A moundlike Buddhist sepulcher, or memorial monument, often erected over a Buddhist relic. ; A grove or clump of trees; as, a toddy tope. ; A small shark or dogfish (Galeorhinus, / Galeus, galeus), native of Europe, but found also on the coasts of California and Tasmania; -- called also toper, oil shark, miller's dog, and penny dog. ; The wren.	N:1u2m,143,2~1u2m,143,2
